----------------------------------------------------------------------

Q: What is a package?
A: A mechanism to group related classes/interfaces and organize
   Java code.

Q: Why use packages?
A: Organization, naming-conflict prevention, access control,
   maintainability, and reuse.

Q: What are access modifiers?
A: Keywords that control the visibility/accessibility of classes
   and members.

Q: What is public?
A: Accessible from anywhere.

Q: What is private?
A: Accessible only within the same class.

Q: What is protected?
A: Accessible within the same package and by subclasses outside
   the package under protected-access rules.

Q: What is default?
A: Package-private; accessible only within the same package.


